  "task": "Assess whether a SageMaker real-time endpoint's production variant is right-sized, given it has no auto-scaling policy and latency spikes at peak.",
  "context": "User says their SageMaker real-time endpoint's production variant has no auto-scaling policy and latency spikes at peak traffic. They ask: is it right-sized? The endpoint name was not given. Agent space account is 123456789012, region us-east-1 (check other associated accounts/regions only if nothing is found). List SageMaker endpoints (InService), and if more than one exists, prioritize those with a variant named 'production' / 'AllTraffic' and no Application Auto Scaling scalable target/policy (verify via application-autoscaling describe_scalable_targets / describe_scaling_policies with ServiceNamespace sagemaker, ResourceId endpoint/<name>/variant/<variant>). Report which endpoint(s) you assessed and why. This is a read-only, focused shallow pass: do not make any mutating calls.",
