  "timeframe": "Last 7 days ending 2026-11-17T19:00:00Z; identify daily peak windows and compare to off-peak baseline (use 1-minute or 5-minute periods around peak)",
  "criteria": "From endpoint config: instance type, InitialInstanceCount, current instance count, variant weights, container/model details, any serverless/concurrency settings, ManagedInstanceScaling or routing strategy. From metrics: peak vs baseline invocations and InvocationsPerInstance, p50/p90/p99 (or Average/Max) ModelLatency and OverheadLatency, CPU/memory/GPU utilization at peak (saturation >70-80%), 4xx/5xx errors and throttling. Conclude whether it is under-provisioned, over-provisioned, or right-sized at baseline but lacking elasticity; say whether latency spikes correlate with load/saturation (queuing -> OverheadLatency up) versus model-side latency. Recommend: instance type/count changes and a target-tracking auto-scaling policy on SageMakerVariantInvocationsPerInstance with a suggested target value derived from observed per-instance throughput at acceptable latency, plus min/max capacity and cooldowns. Note evidence limits clearly. Keep the final report concise with concrete numbers."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Assess SageMaker endpoint sizing and peak-time latency"}], "created_at": null}

